{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 408785, "name": "Gerson Parsey", "username": "gerson", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-05-31T13:37:01.601Z", "cooked": "<p>conky: llua_do_call: function conky_main execution failed: /home/linux/Serene-Conky/Core/main.lua:55: attempt to call a nil value (global ‘cairo_xlib_surface_create’)</p>\n<p>I already have cairo I have my lua in the system, I tried to use conky but I somehow couldn’t get it to work.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2025-05-31T13:37:01.601Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 916, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 4589.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 154849, "topic_slug": "issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42", "display_username": "Gerson Parsey", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 27100, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42/154849/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 408788, "name": "George N. White III", "username": "gnwiii", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/gnwiii/{size}/34440_2.png", "created_at": "2025-05-31T13:49:11.336Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"gerson\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"154849\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/294172/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Gerson Parsey:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>main.lua:55: attempt to call a nil value (global ‘cairo_xlib_surface_create’)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>See: <a href=\"https://github.com/brndnmtthws/conky/issues/1978\">Conky Gihub Issue 1978</a> from last summer.</p>\n<p>Looks like Conkly is not being maintained in Fedora as the current package is from Fedora 31.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">Available packages\nName           : conky\nEpoch          : 0\nVersion        : 1.22.0\nRelease        : 1.fc41\nArchitecture   : x86_64\nDownload size  : 740.0 KiB\nInstalled size : 1.7 MiB\nSource         : conky-1.22.0-1.fc41.src.rpm\nRepository     : updates\nSummary        : A system monitor for X\nURL            : https://github.com/brndnmtthws/conky\nLicense        : GPL-3.0-or-later AND LGPL-2.1-or-later AND MIT-open-group AND BSD-3-Clause\nDescription    : A system monitor for X originally based on the torsmo code. but more kickass.\n               : It just keeps on given'er. Yeah.\nVendor         : Fedora Project\n</code></pre>\n<p>Maybe <a href=\"https://alternativeto.net/software/conky/?platform=linux\">one of the Alternativeto.net suggestions </a> will meet your needs.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2025-05-31T13:49:11.336Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 26, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 154.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 154849, "topic_slug": "issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42", "display_username": "George N. White III", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://alternativeto.net/software/conky/?platform=linux", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "clicks": 40}, {"url": "https://github.com/brndnmtthws/conky/issues/1978", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "[Bug]: cairo_xlib_surface_create nil value error with Lua Cairo · Issue #1978 · brndnmtthws/conky · GitHub", "clicks": 24}], "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4552, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42/154849/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 408805, "name": "Gerson Parsey", "username": "gerson", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-05-31T16:18:11.377Z", "cooked": "<p>Okay.. your reply is highly appreciated. <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/+1.png?v=14\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2025-05-31T16:18:11.377Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 21, "readers_count": 20, "score": 4.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 154849, "topic_slug": "issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42", "display_username": "Gerson Parsey", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 4552, "username": "gnwiii", "name": "George N. White III", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/gnwiii/{size}/34440_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 27100, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42/154849/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 422665, "name": "Oleks Podoleks", "username": "witcher619", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/w/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-07-21T13:07:06.000Z", "cooked": "<p>Hey!<br>\nHas this even been fixed?<br>\nI’m currently trying to install conky and apply certain themes, and while generally the app works fine, the circles that are present in both themes don’t appear at all no matter what I do.<br>\nI thought there were some mistakes in the .conf files probably, but the only error that I get when I start the .conf files is attempt to call a nil value (global ‘cairo_xlib_surface_create’), so I googled this error, found the github thread, it seemed too old for me, then I found this thread from maj 2025, i.e. very recent, but George referenced that very same github occurrence.<br>\nSo I’m wondering whether it has been broken for such a long time? Seems so odd, how is it even possible? I’m perplexed.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2025-07-21T13:07:06.000Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 4, "reads": 17, "readers_count": 16, "score": 28.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 154849, "topic_slug": "issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42", "display_username": "Oleks Podoleks", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 28377, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42/154849/4", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 422674, "name": "George N. White III", "username": "gnwiii", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/gnwiii/{size}/34440_2.png", "created_at": "2025-07-21T13:38:41.548Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"witcher619\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"154849\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/w/294172/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Oleks Podoleks:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So I’m wondering whether it has been broken for such a long time? Seems so odd, how is it even possible?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It is not unusual for older packages to go unmaintained: a better alternative is available, or the original developer moves on to other projects or an isolated location, etc.   If the package has a large user community, someone may step forward to maintain it, but apparently this has not happened.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2025-07-21T13:38:41.548Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 4, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 16, "reads": 16, "readers_count": 15, "score": 88.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 154849, "topic_slug": "issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42", "display_username": "George N. White III", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 28377, "username": "witcher619", "name": "Oleks Podoleks", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/w/294172/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4552, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42/154849/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 422680, "name": "P G", "username": "pg-tips", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-07-21T13:47:45.694Z", "cooked": "<p>There’s a Fedora 42 package and it seems at least somewhat maintained (e.g. maintainer activity from June 2025 here: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2369338\" class=\"inline-onebox\">2369338 – Conky is not build with Wayland Support</a>).</p>\n<p>Without prior knowledge, I found the Github issue not easy to follow - I don’t know if it was resolved by some change in how Conky is built, or whether the idea is that the user should change their Lua script to add a <code>require</code> statement.</p>\n<p>If the resolution was a code change or build flag change that affects the package, it would be worth raising a ticket in Red Hat Bugzilla.</p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2025-07-21T13:47:45.694Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 5, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 6, "reads": 14, "readers_count": 13, "score": 37.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 154849, "topic_slug": "issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42", "display_username": "P G", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2369338", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "2369338 – Conky is not build with Wayland Support", "clicks": 39}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 4552, "username": "gnwiii", "name": "George N. White III", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/gnwiii/{size}/34440_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 25377, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42/154849/6", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 422871, "name": "Oleks Podoleks", "username": "witcher619", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/w/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-07-21T21:10:09.391Z", "cooked": "<p>Thanks for your quick replies.<br>\nI’m actually using EndeavourOS, so please don’t call me an impostor, but this was the only forum where I saw conky being discussed recently, so I decided to register and follow up on this thread.<br>\nI’ve managed to get rid of the stated error with the help of ChatGBP and some references from the forum posts linked in the github page. The error was gone by adding the following parameters before the start of the lua function:<br>\nrequire ‘cairo’<br>\nrequire ‘cairo_xlib’ – <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/backhand_index_pointing_left.png?v=14\" title=\":backhand_index_pointing_left:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":backhand_index_pointing_left:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> This is the crucial fix</p>\n<p>Then I was grappling for another 2 hours with rings actually being drawn, but that’s another conversation xD</p>\n<p>This conky is really clunky <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/frowning.png?v=14\" title=\":frowning:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":frowning:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2025-07-21T21:10:09.391Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 6, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 12, "reads": 13, "readers_count": 12, "score": 62.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 154849, "topic_slug": "issue-running-conky-on-my-fedora-42", "display_username": "Oleks Podoleks", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flai